From 8cf8c1d9fdd0b71118e8de5a9ad34178c5cafde8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:34:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [AdaptiveStream] Keep the last frames of the old quality at a
 quality change

At a change of the representation, ensureSegment returned false at the end
of the old data and notified the session. The TS reader then returned one of
the frames that it keeps, but DemuxRead returned the stream change in place
of that frame, and the reopen deleted the reader with the other kept frames.
A TS stream lost two video frames at each quality change, and the audio
frames that waited for a PTS. A read before the reopen also read the data of
the new representation into the reader of the old representation.

- After the notification, the old representation has no more data and waits
  for no segment, until the reopen (start_stream) or a seek. A seek clears
  the state, so that the reopen continues in the segment of the seek.
- The session signals the change only after the reader of the old
  representation returned all frames (EOS). DemuxRead checks the change
  also when no stream has a next sample, because the old reader can be the
  only stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
